摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Cross-device agent workspace sync for OpenCode, Codex, and DeepSeek Harness — backup, restore, update, and configuration inspection.","id":"gh:1266465567","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"uagent-sync","slug":"severin-ye/uagent-sync","topics":["agent-tools","backup","codex","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","opencode","restore","workspace-sync"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Cross-device agent workspace sync for OpenCode, Codex, and DeepSeek Harness — backup, restore, updat"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"e, and configuration inspection."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"> **Node compatibility:** 3.1.0 requires `^22.22.2 || ^24.15.0 || >=26.0.0`, matching its locked pro"},{"id":"p2s2","text":"duction dependencies. Node 18 results are historical and do not establish supported installation. Se"},{"id":"p2s3","text":"e the exact compatibility boundary."},{"id":"p3s1","text":"uagent-sync"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"One command to backup. One command to restore. Your entire dev environment, synced across machines."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Export your agent workspace — submodules, configs, skills, API keys — to a private GitHub repo."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"On a new machine, pull it back and everything installs itself."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Why?"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"You have multiple machines. Each runs opencode and/or Codex with different plugins, MCP servers, ski"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"lls, and submodules checked out at different commits. Keeping them in sync is a nightmare of `git su"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"bmodule update`, `npx skills add`, and copy-pasting config files."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"**uagent-sync** makes it a single command:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"That's it. Submodules reset to exact commits. MCP servers rebuilt. Skills reinstalled. Config merged"},{"id":"p11s2","text":". API keys templated. Everything just works."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"uagent-sync ships one CLI and three agent entry points. Install the one you use:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"### OpenCode"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"For OpenCode V1, keep the existing file entry in `config/opencode.json`:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"For OpenCode V2, use its native entry instead:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"A local checkout can use the **directory** `/absolute/path/to/uagent-sync/dist/plugin-v2` after buil"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"ding. V2 skips configured JavaScript file paths. The V2 entry registers the same 16 tools and packag"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"ed skills, sharing their validation and business logic with V1; it does not perform a backup or upda"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"te merely by loading. Existing V1 configuration and the default package export remain supported."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"### Codex"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"### Codex extension deduplication"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Migration analysis is the single Dashboard module for coverage/gaps, compatibility, functional overl"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"ap/deduplication, migration decisions, and execution verification. Choose either `uagent-sync dashbo"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"ard --page migration-analysis` with a single Agent (functional duplicates) or an explicit source/tar"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"get pair (migration comparison); no scope means no comparison scan. Sources are labeled official, th"},{"id":"p26s5","text":"ird-party, local, or unknown, and official provenance requires controlled install evidence. The `age"},{"id":"p26s6","text":"nt-browser → browser/chrome` mapping is one grouped review item with multiple evidence edges."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"The V1 audit ledger `usync-dotfiles/agents/codex/policies/extension-conflicts.json` is never changed"},{"id":"p27s2","text":" by scans. New confirmed decisions use `usync-dotfiles/policies/capability-decisions.json`; creation"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"/import happens inside the first write transaction. Codex changes require a staged decision, exact b"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"yte-preserving config/ledger diff, and a second confirmation with a one-use token. Timestamped backu"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"ps are created; restart Codex after applying. OpenCode and DeepSeek are always read-only, and no ext"},{"id":"p27s6","text":"ension is uninstalled or deleted. The legacy extension write endpoint is disabled; `/extension-confl"},{"id":"p27s7","text":"icts` is a compatibility alias for the unified Dashboard."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"### Explain the last update"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"### First backup"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"### What you get after installing"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"- **5 skills**: `uagent-sync-backup` (backup workflow), `uagent-sync-restore` (new-device restore), "},{"id":"p34s2","text":"`uagent-sync-update` (ecosystem update), `uagent-sync-device` (device profiles), `uagent-sync-crysta"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"llize` (installation provenance) — loaded on demand, guiding the agent to use the CLI\n- **SessionSta"},{"id":"p34s4","text":"rt hook**: injects CLI usage hints at session start (`PLUGIN_ROOT` resolves the plugin root; on Wind"},{"id":"p34s5","text":"ows it goes through a Git-bash wrapper)\n- **CLI (the single execution channel)**: `node <plugin>/dis"},{"id":"p34s6","text":"t/cli.js <command>` — workspace commands shared with the opencode plugin"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"### How it works"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## What It Syncs"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"| Category | What | How |"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"| **Submodules** | All repos, exact commit hash | `git clone` + `git reset --hard` |\n| **OpenCode Co"},{"id":"p39s2","text":"nfig** | plugins, MCP servers, providers | Deep-merge, never overwrite |\n| **Skills** | Installed sk"},{"id":"p39s3","text":"ills from git sources | `skills add <source> -g` |\n| **API Keys** | Names + descriptions (never valu"},{"id":"p39s4","text":"es) | Template file at `keys/API.md` — the `keys/` directory is gitignored in `usync-dotfiles`, so r"},{"id":"p39s5","text":"eal values only ever exist locally |\n| **Dependencies** | gh CLI, Ralph, Skills CLI | Auto-install v"},{"id":"p39s6","text":"ia winget/brew/apt/npm |\n| **Windows Fixes** | NTFS path issues | Auto-detects problematic filenames"},{"id":"p39s7","text":", applies `git config core.protectNTFS` |\n| **Install Log** | Every install, its source, any pitfall"},{"id":"p39s8","text":"s | `state/install-log.json` — provenance you can trust |"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"> **Code never touches data.** The plugin lives in one directory. All generated files go to `usync-d"},{"id":"p42s2","text":"otfiles/`. Clean separation."},{"id":"p43s1","text":"The implemented dependency direction is **Entry → Application → Domain/Ports ← Adapters**. `Workspac"},{"id":"p43s2","text":"eState` v3 is the validated in-memory read contract; current wire exports remain backward-compatible"},{"id":"p43s3","text":". DSH and `all` restore scopes fail closed because they do not yet have restore writers/contracts. S"},{"id":"p43s4","text":"ee docs/ARCHITECTURE.md for concrete boundaries, Codex-only isolation, permanent `codebase-memory-mc"},{"id":"p43s5","text":"p` deletion, and the runtime scanner extension boundary. A supported fourth Agent still requires exp"},{"id":"p43s6","text":"licit AgentId, paths, Dashboard, migration-context, and host-contract work."},{"id":"p44s1","text":"## Security"},{"id":"p45s1","text":"- **Command injection hardened**: `shellEscape()` wraps all user input before shell execution. Git c"},{"id":"p45s2","text":"ommits use `-F` file input instead of `-m` string interpolation.\n- **Path traversal guarded**: `isPa"},{"id":"p45s3","text":"thSafe()` validates all file paths resolve within workspace root.\n- **Zod schema enforced**: Every i"},{"id":"p45s4","text":"nput validated with `.min()`, `.max()`, `.strict()` before touching the filesystem.\n- **Secrets neve"},{"id":"p45s5","text":"r exported**: Only environment variable _names_ are recorded. Values stay on your machine.\n- **Priva"},{"id":"p45s6","text":"te repos by default**: `create_repo` creates `--private`. Warns if existing repo is public."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
